    "howto": {
      "title": "How dispatch works",
      "body": {
        "type": "column",
        "scroll": true,
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "style": "title",
            "value": "Projects, tasks and logs"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Dispatch tracks your team's work in three levels:\n\n• PROJECT — a folder of work. Projects can hold SUB-PROJECTS, so the left column is a directory you can expand like folders.\n• TASK — something to do inside a project (middle column). Tasks can hold SUB-TASKS — they nest right under their parent in the tasks column (⋮ on a task → New sub-task here).\n• LOG — a task's running conversation: comments and attachments (right panel).\n\nTo use it: pick a project in the directory, pick a task in the middle, then read or add to its log on the right. The directory never shows log comments — those live with their task.\n\nA project travels: its ⋮ menu can EXPORT the whole project (sub-projects, tasks, logs and attachments) as one file, and IMPORT such a file into another project — or another device."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "style": "title",
            "value": "Logs can hold more than text"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A log entry is a COMMENT — no title, just what you want to say. Each one shows who wrote it and when.\n\nComments THREAD: tap Reply on a comment to answer it, and replies are full comments too — they can hold their own replies and attachments, as deep as the conversation goes.\n\nATTACHMENTS are the things a comment (or the task itself) houses:\n• a file or image (paperclip),\n• a wireframe / sheet / doc / sketch — a live tool with its OWN data.\n\nAttachments show as small tiles. Tap one and it opens FULL-SCREEN — work in it, then come back to the log. Use Attach… on a comment's ⋮ menu, or the composer's tool button for the task."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "style": "title",
            "value": "One task, more than one project"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A task doesn't have to live in just one place. Drag a task onto another project to LINK it there too — it's the same task shown in both, so editing it once updates it everywhere. A little badge shows when a task lives in more than one project."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "inbox": {
      "title": "Inbox",
      "body": {
        "type": "column",
        "scroll": true,
        "crossAxis": "stretch",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "style": "caption",
            "value": "Open turns — comments still waiting on a reply. The chip on each shows who it's directed at and who wrote it. Swipe (or use the ⋮ menu) to mark one answered; tap to open it."
          },
          {
            "type": "cards",
            "table": "entries",
            "title": "comment",
            "expandable": false,
            "filter": {
              "column": "awaiting",
              "value": true
            },
            "tags": [
              {
                "column": "prompting"
              },
              {
                "column": "createdBy"
              }
            ],
            "swipeActions": [
              {
                "label": "Mark answered",
                "icon": "check",
                "action": {
                  "fn": "toggleField",
                  "args": {
                    "table": "entries",
                    "column": "awaiting"
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "action": {
              "fn": "editRow",
              "args": {
                "table": "entries"
              }
            },
            "emptyTitle": "Nothing awaiting a reply",
            "emptyText": "When you address a comment to someone (the “to:” chip on the composer), it lands here as an open turn until it’s marked answered."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "plan": {
